## iboxreplica ACTIVE_ACTIVE examples

these examples only work for fc and iscsi protocols!

edit and create these to test iboxreplica controller logic, these examples are for ACTIVE_ACTIVE replication type.  You
can create a replica based on a VOLUME, or CG using ACTIVE_ACTIVE replication type. Unlike ASYNC replication type, filesystem entity types are not supported with ACTIVE_ACTIVE replication type.

The 'local_entity-name' is the PV (volume) name that you want to replicate.

The 'link_remote_system_name' has to be looked up using the Ibox API (get links) call.  This is the name
given to the link, not always the same as the remote ibox host name.

The 'remote_pool_id' has to be looked up on the remote ibox host using the Ibox API prior to creating
the iboxreplica resource.  

Unlike ASYNC replication type, the 'sync_interval' or 'rpo_value' settings are not used for ACTIVE_ACTIVE 
replication type and should not be included in the resource yaml.

